   "description": "Bright White Blooms When the Rest of the Garden is Winding DownJust Chill\u00ae Double White Camellia opens thick-petaled, pure white flowers in fall, right when most shrubs have called it a season. The blooms carry a light fragrance and stand out beautifully against glossy emerald-green foliage that holds its color all year.This series was selected for improved cold hardiness, so gardeners with a little more chill in the air can finally grow camellias with confidence. At 5 to 8 feet tall with an upright habit, it works as an evergreen hedge, a middle-of-the-border anchor, or a thriller in a large patio container you can tuck against a sheltered wall for winter.Why You&#39;ll Love the Just Chill\u00ae Double White CamelliaFall and winter interest: bright white double flowers appear in autumn, plus year-round evergreen structure.Improved cold hardiness: bred to handle colder winters than traditional camellias.Fragrant blooms: a subtle sweet scent near walkways, patios, and entries.Deer resistant and disease resistant: less browsing damage and less fuss for you.Hedge-worthy habit: upright, densely leaved growth makes an easy evergreen privacy screen.Plant it where you&#39;ll see it in November, and it will pay you back every fall.",
